00:01:43,190 --> 00:01:46,370
[Previously on KNOT]

27
00:01:43,340 --> 00:01:45,690
No matter what happened in the past,

28
00:01:45,690 --> 00:01:47,009
Naphitch is still

29
00:01:47,030 --> 00:01:48,509
a member of this family.

30
00:01:48,530 --> 00:01:50,530
How can you let him take my wife away?

31
00:01:50,910 --> 00:01:53,240
Who dares to disobey your father-in-law?

32
00:01:53,960 --> 00:01:54,970
Then I...

33
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:57,270
have nothing to hide.

34
00:02:36,300 --> 00:02:37,079
Yes.

35
00:02:37,100 --> 00:02:38,280
I think it's okay.

36
00:03:17,260 --> 00:03:18,460
Are you tired?

37
00:03:18,490 --> 00:03:20,620
You've been preparing since morning.

38
00:03:21,050 --> 00:03:22,180
I'm not tired at all.

39
00:03:23,060 --> 00:03:24,860
I'm more excited than anything.

40
00:03:25,560 --> 00:03:26,880
I never thought

41
00:03:26,900 --> 00:03:28,950
my little cafe

42
00:03:29,450 --> 00:03:31,710
could take part in an event of this level.

43
00:03:44,020 --> 00:03:46,090
Do I look weird wearing this?

44
00:03:46,430 --> 00:03:47,290
Nakhin...

45
00:03:57,440 --> 00:03:59,370
I'm afraid the people at the event,

46
00:04:00,090 --> 00:04:01,870
especially those Alphas,

47
00:04:02,850 --> 00:04:04,980
will think I'm not good enough for you.

48
00:04:16,380 --> 00:04:18,220
Raise your head, Ongsa.

49
00:04:19,490 --> 00:04:20,940
I told you,

50
00:04:21,690 --> 00:04:23,300
don't put anyone's opinion

51
00:04:24,190 --> 00:04:25,990
above my heart.

52
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:30,910
To me,

53
00:04:32,150 --> 00:04:34,750
you're not just the person
standing beside me.

54
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:36,860
You are my honor.

55
00:04:38,470 --> 00:04:40,310
You are my pride.

56
00:04:42,850 --> 00:04:44,230
You are the one

57
00:04:44,990 --> 00:04:46,420
I chose myself.

58
00:04:49,540 --> 00:04:51,450
And tonight everyone will know

59
00:04:52,659 --> 00:04:54,390
that I, a True Alpha, chose you.

60
00:04:55,220 --> 00:04:56,750
Not because of pheromones,

61
00:04:57,440 --> 00:04:59,470
not because of secondary gender,

62
00:04:59,490 --> 00:05:02,340
not because of some ridiculous fate,

63
00:05:10,280 --> 00:05:12,110
but because you are you, Ongsa.

64
00:05:13,680 --> 00:05:15,190
And in this world,

65
00:05:17,080 --> 00:05:18,640
no one can replace you.

66
00:05:21,870 --> 00:05:23,710
Your words

67
00:05:24,500 --> 00:05:26,360
always make my heart race.

68
00:05:28,670 --> 00:05:29,490
That's good.

69
00:05:31,440 --> 00:05:32,560
Because I don't want

70
00:05:32,560 --> 00:05:35,020
you to just stand beside me
like anyone else.

71
00:05:39,430 --> 00:05:41,159
Then how do you want me to stand?

72
00:05:42,980 --> 00:05:44,909
Stand

73
00:05:46,170 --> 00:05:47,970
where no one can touch,

74
00:05:50,250 --> 00:05:51,810
as Nakhin's person.

75
00:05:53,930 --> 00:05:55,330
Sounds good, doesn't it?

76
00:05:58,580 --> 00:06:00,500
Since you put it that way,

77
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:03,160
I can't escape.

78
00:06:04,640 --> 00:06:06,700
Who said I was going to let you escape?

79
00:06:36,340 --> 00:06:38,900
Hello, Ms. Amintra.

80
00:06:39,310 --> 00:06:40,400
Hello.

81
00:06:42,210 --> 00:06:43,870
Go take care of Kingyok first.

82
00:06:52,670 --> 00:06:54,200
Do you have anything to say?

83
00:06:55,590 --> 00:06:58,130
Seems we can finally

84
00:06:58,150 --> 00:06:59,490
talk openly and honestly for once.

85
00:06:59,490 --> 00:07:01,050
Sounds like good news.

86
00:07:01,080 --> 00:07:03,140
There's no problem
on my mother's side anymore.

87
00:07:03,140 --> 00:07:06,040
After learning your mom and dad divorced,

88
00:07:06,610 --> 00:07:08,280
my mom didn't mind anything.

89
00:07:08,300 --> 00:07:10,120
She even said

90
00:07:10,160 --> 00:07:11,820
she feels sorry for your mother.

91
00:07:11,820 --> 00:07:14,990
If she were forced to marry someone,

92
00:07:15,010 --> 00:07:16,680
she'd be unhappy too.

93
00:07:16,710 --> 00:07:17,810
So now, we can

94
00:07:17,830 --> 00:07:20,320
finally be honest and be friends.

95
00:07:23,460 --> 00:07:24,330
That's good.

96
00:07:25,450 --> 00:07:27,180
Is that all you're going to say?

97
00:07:27,500 --> 00:07:29,560
I don't know what long speech to make.

98
00:07:30,290 --> 00:07:31,080
Then...

99
00:07:31,670 --> 00:07:35,200
let's wish this new friendship
doesn't break too easily.

100
00:07:36,909 --> 00:07:39,640
It wouldn't have broken
if you hadn't started it.

101
00:07:40,640 --> 00:07:42,290
I'll try my best.

102
00:08:38,760 --> 00:08:39,679
Mr. Nakhun,

103
00:08:39,700 --> 00:08:41,520
appearing so publicly today,

104
00:08:41,539 --> 00:08:43,789
does that mean good news is coming soon?

105
00:08:45,990 --> 00:08:47,470
If by good news

106
00:08:48,050 --> 00:08:49,470
you mean marriage,

107
00:08:51,660 --> 00:08:53,210
then it depends on when Phatsa

108
00:08:53,210 --> 00:08:54,260
is ready.

109
00:08:55,970 --> 00:08:57,080
In that case,

110
00:08:57,110 --> 00:08:58,650
if Mr. Phatsa is ready,

111
00:08:58,680 --> 00:09:00,320
when would it be, Mr. Nakhun?

112
00:09:01,480 --> 00:09:04,000
As long as Phatsa is ready,

113
00:09:04,730 --> 00:09:06,130
we could marry tomorrow.

114
00:09:08,340 --> 00:09:09,860
You're exaggerating.

115
00:09:10,440 --> 00:09:11,610
I'm not.

116
00:09:12,330 --> 00:09:13,610
I'm serious.

117
00:09:15,200 --> 00:09:16,230
Then hurry up and get married.

118
00:09:16,230 --> 00:09:17,260
I'm waiting!

119
00:09:22,990 --> 00:09:24,920
Which family were they from again?

120
00:09:26,070 --> 00:09:27,200
We'll ask later.

121
00:09:35,690 --> 00:09:37,210
Happy birthday.

122
00:09:41,550 --> 00:09:42,680
Thank you very much.

123
00:09:44,380 --> 00:09:45,640
And congratulations.

124
00:09:46,910 --> 00:09:49,910
About that piece of land...

125
00:09:50,350 --> 00:09:52,540
If those troubles hadn't happened before,

126
00:09:52,540 --> 00:09:56,290
I think the competition between us
would've been more interesting.

127
00:09:56,290 --> 00:09:57,600
I won't lose to you.

128
00:09:58,560 --> 00:10:00,480
Good, I'll be waiting.

129
00:10:06,340 --> 00:10:08,080
I'll take my leave now.

130
00:10:09,370 --> 00:10:10,130
Enjoy.

131
00:10:21,980 --> 00:10:23,240
Let's go.

132
00:10:24,230 --> 00:10:26,690
I'll go out first
and chat with some friends.

133
00:10:41,960 --> 00:10:43,300
I never imagined

134
00:10:43,330 --> 00:10:44,740
there'd be a day we could stand together

135
00:10:44,740 --> 00:10:46,530
and chat so calmly like this.

136
00:10:46,550 --> 00:10:49,120
Yeah, before,

137
00:10:49,150 --> 00:10:51,080
I was always busy comparing myself to you.

138
00:10:51,080 --> 00:10:53,810
Comparing family background,
and children too.

139
00:10:56,990 --> 00:10:58,390
Speaking of which,

140
00:10:58,410 --> 00:11:00,540
those two kids were quite mischievous too.

141
00:11:00,540 --> 00:11:03,240
They secretly grew close
since third grade,

142
00:11:03,840 --> 00:11:06,210
and we had no idea at all.

143
00:11:09,010 --> 00:11:10,840
If you're free,

144
00:11:10,860 --> 00:11:13,120
you're welcome to come to my home for tea.

145
00:11:13,400 --> 00:11:15,420
Thank you for the invitation.

146
00:11:16,090 --> 00:11:18,500
I'll be waiting for you.

147
00:11:26,880 --> 00:11:28,900
Mom always played her role well,

148
00:11:29,450 --> 00:11:31,490
but now she looks much happier.

149
00:11:31,760 --> 00:11:34,310
Yes, true happiness

150
00:11:35,070 --> 00:11:36,750
can't be hidden.

151
00:11:49,150 --> 00:11:51,050
Today, thank you all

152
00:11:51,470 --> 00:11:52,270
for coming

153
00:11:52,660 --> 00:11:54,230
to me

154
00:11:54,500 --> 00:11:56,230
and the Devathitirat family's

155
00:11:56,270 --> 00:11:58,070
absolutely wonderful evening.

156
00:12:01,590 --> 00:12:03,640
Today, I also have something important

157
00:12:03,640 --> 00:12:05,050
to announce.

158
00:12:05,610 --> 00:12:07,650
It's not just about my birthday.

159
00:12:09,250 --> 00:12:10,910
It is also a new starting point

160
00:12:12,520 --> 00:12:14,120
for the Devathitirat family

161
00:12:14,510 --> 00:12:16,510
and the next step toward the future.

162
00:12:18,190 --> 00:12:19,420
From now on,

163
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:21,550
Devathitirat

164
00:12:22,200 --> 00:12:24,520
will no longer be managed by one person.

165
00:12:25,870 --> 00:12:27,330
I hereby invite Mr. Nakhin

166
00:12:28,190 --> 00:12:29,960
as Executive Vice President,

167
00:12:38,990 --> 00:12:40,080
and another,

168
00:12:41,940 --> 00:12:43,190
Mr. Naphitch,

169
00:12:43,460 --> 00:12:45,970
as Vice President of Business Support.

170
00:12:53,680 --> 00:12:55,290
Finally,

171
00:12:55,650 --> 00:12:57,400
I would like to invite everyone

172
00:12:57,810 --> 00:12:59,970
to make a toast for this shining night.

173
00:13:00,970 --> 00:13:02,120
Cheers.

174
00:13:15,170 --> 00:13:16,360
Well said.

175
00:13:17,310 --> 00:13:18,150
You can do it.

176
00:13:18,170 --> 00:13:19,970
Trust yourself.

177
00:13:40,320 --> 00:13:42,610
My legs are sore from standing
to greet the guests.

178
00:13:42,610 --> 00:13:43,610
Just bear with it.

179
00:13:44,200 --> 00:13:46,500
This is your future husband's event.

180
00:13:48,410 --> 00:13:50,110
What are you talking about?

181
00:13:50,750 --> 00:13:52,750
My dad won't even let us get married.

182
00:13:54,420 --> 00:13:56,350
Your dad is way too old-fashioned.

183
00:13:57,120 --> 00:13:58,290
These days,

184
00:13:58,320 --> 00:14:00,650
who still waits for the elders' approval?

185
00:14:01,750 --> 00:14:03,500
Not every family is like this.

186
00:14:07,200 --> 00:14:10,140
Then if you got pregnant before marriage,

187
00:14:10,160 --> 00:14:12,230
wouldn't your dad be even more furious?

188
00:14:12,230 --> 00:14:13,420
Ongsa.

189
00:14:20,100 --> 00:14:23,480
Actually, Nakhun wants a baby too.

190
00:14:25,490 --> 00:14:27,090
If everything settles down,

191
00:14:28,710 --> 00:14:30,570
having one right away is fine too.

192
00:14:30,910 --> 00:14:33,350
Oh ho...

193
00:14:36,500 --> 00:14:37,920
Stop laughing.

194
00:14:50,360 --> 00:14:51,680
I never thought

195
00:14:52,910 --> 00:14:55,110
Naphitch would do something like that.

196
00:14:57,460 --> 00:14:58,740
At that time, Saengnuea

197
00:14:58,740 --> 00:14:59,470
lost his mind

198
00:15:00,810 --> 00:15:03,110
and tried to force Nakhin into Heat.

199
00:15:03,920 --> 00:15:05,240
But in the end,

200
00:15:05,950 --> 00:15:07,720
no one gained anything.

201
00:15:33,290 --> 00:15:34,560
If you do this,

202
00:15:36,080 --> 00:15:38,060
you'll make yourself a joke too.

203
00:15:40,080 --> 00:15:41,470
I don't care.

204
00:15:43,390 --> 00:15:44,810
Because I'm an Alpha.

205
00:15:46,260 --> 00:15:48,720
Alpha was born stronger
than other genders.

206
00:15:49,520 --> 00:15:51,140
No matter what happens,

207
00:15:51,760 --> 00:15:53,490
an Alpha always has a way out.

208
00:15:54,640 --> 00:15:56,500
We still have the right to choose.

209
00:15:57,270 --> 00:15:58,280
We can still

210
00:15:59,500 --> 00:16:01,220
sleep with others.

211
00:16:02,330 --> 00:16:03,790
But Omegas are different.

212
00:16:04,740 --> 00:16:06,750
An Omega that has been bitten

213
00:16:07,400 --> 00:16:10,200
can no longer have anything to do
with anyone else.

214
00:16:10,280 --> 00:16:12,140
This is the rule of forming a bond.

215
00:16:17,930 --> 00:16:18,850
See?

216
00:16:20,540 --> 00:16:22,570
In the end,

217
00:16:23,360 --> 00:16:24,840
it's exactly as I thought.

218
00:16:26,690 --> 00:16:27,810
Why

219
00:16:29,360 --> 00:16:31,170
must an Omega like me

220
00:16:31,560 --> 00:16:33,270
stay at the very bottom?

221
00:16:35,280 --> 00:16:37,710
I just want to have my own life.

222
00:16:40,730 --> 00:16:43,140
Why was I born an Omega?

223
00:16:49,230 --> 00:16:50,450
Because you

224
00:16:50,880 --> 00:16:53,400
only stare at the things
pressing you down.

225
00:16:54,830 --> 00:16:56,060
Being an Omega

226
00:16:56,940 --> 00:16:59,590
doesn't mean the ending
is always like that.

227
00:17:01,550 --> 00:17:03,040
If you don't believe me,

228
00:17:07,220 --> 00:17:08,940
look at Phatsa.

229
00:17:11,180 --> 00:17:12,420
Look at my mother.

230
00:17:31,720 --> 00:17:33,140
Being an Omega

231
00:17:34,220 --> 00:17:35,990
doesn't mean

232
00:17:37,010 --> 00:17:38,810
you can't succeed.

233
00:17:40,280 --> 00:17:41,770
It also doesn't mean you

234
00:17:42,510 --> 00:17:44,960
must forever surrender to fate.

235
00:18:04,120 --> 00:18:05,040
In the end,

236
00:18:07,900 --> 00:18:10,430
whether you choose to see yourself
as a victim

237
00:18:11,440 --> 00:18:12,960
or stand up and fight again

238
00:18:14,450 --> 00:18:15,900
depends only on you.

239
00:19:25,150 --> 00:19:26,010
Have a seat.

240
00:19:35,400 --> 00:19:36,350
Look at this.

241
00:19:43,620 --> 00:19:45,290
What is it now?

242
00:19:45,930 --> 00:19:47,680
I'm tired today.

243
00:19:47,710 --> 00:19:49,660
Can we look tomorrow?

244
00:19:52,340 --> 00:19:53,620
Just look today.

245
00:19:54,640 --> 00:19:56,570
Otherwise I won't be able to sleep.

246
00:20:08,230 --> 00:20:09,420
Wait.

247
00:20:10,180 --> 00:20:11,950
Real Estate Development.

248
00:20:13,050 --> 00:20:14,920
Executive Vice President.

249
00:20:17,490 --> 00:20:19,060
Are you crazy?

250
00:20:20,050 --> 00:20:21,850
I just graduated.

251
00:20:22,640 --> 00:20:24,020
I'm inexperienced.

252
00:20:26,440 --> 00:20:27,920
But you're smart, Phatsa.

253
00:20:28,950 --> 00:20:30,000
I think

254
00:20:30,990 --> 00:20:33,740
learning while managing

255
00:20:34,100 --> 00:20:35,790
is nothing to worry about.

256
00:20:38,050 --> 00:20:39,580
Are you really not worried?

257
00:20:40,970 --> 00:20:42,410
If...

258
00:20:43,540 --> 00:20:45,540
I ruin the company,

259
00:20:47,770 --> 00:20:49,730
your dad will definitely kill me.

260
00:20:55,880 --> 00:20:57,080
This position was proposed

261
00:20:57,080 --> 00:20:58,480
to Phatsa by Dad himself.

262
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:01,150
He also signed

263
00:21:02,710 --> 00:21:04,170
these documents himself.

264
00:21:12,460 --> 00:21:13,590
Really?

265
00:21:20,650 --> 00:21:22,140
Dad wants to rest.

266
00:21:23,320 --> 00:21:25,120
He wants to let go of everything.

267
00:21:26,140 --> 00:21:27,000
Now he's moved to

268
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:28,800
Naphitch's mother's old house,

269
00:21:29,710 --> 00:21:31,530
spending more time alone,

270
00:21:32,260 --> 00:21:33,790
slowing down his thoughts,

271
00:21:34,610 --> 00:21:35,590
and

272
00:21:36,520 --> 00:21:39,120
trying to become a better person
than he is now.

273
00:21:40,340 --> 00:21:41,930
After that incident,

274
00:21:43,430 --> 00:21:44,840
he hopes

275
00:21:46,670 --> 00:21:48,200
he can become a grandfather

276
00:21:48,930 --> 00:21:50,590
who makes his grandson proud.

277
00:22:00,180 --> 00:22:01,390
Actually,

278
00:22:03,270 --> 00:22:04,840
your dad is impressive.

279
00:22:06,370 --> 00:22:07,210
Although

280
00:22:08,690 --> 00:22:11,040
sometimes he is too self-centered

281
00:22:11,460 --> 00:22:13,540
and a bit domineering,

282
00:22:15,200 --> 00:22:17,110
he is admirable

283
00:22:18,370 --> 00:22:19,630
and worthy of respect.

284
00:22:20,500 --> 00:22:22,430
The company got to where it is today

285
00:22:23,930 --> 00:22:25,470
thanks to his ability.

286
00:22:26,870 --> 00:22:28,630
And another thing is

287
00:22:29,270 --> 00:22:32,550
there were some things
he didn't have to step in and help with,

288
00:22:32,550 --> 00:22:33,870
but he chose to do so.

289
00:22:35,570 --> 00:22:36,760
For example,

290
00:22:38,100 --> 00:22:40,160
he chose to help Saengnuea's father.

291
00:22:42,090 --> 00:22:43,450
As businessmen,

292
00:22:44,540 --> 00:22:45,670
we must have ability

293
00:22:46,610 --> 00:22:47,790
and also kindness.

294
00:22:49,860 --> 00:22:51,080
This world

295
00:22:52,380 --> 00:22:53,690
runs on balance.

296
00:22:55,460 --> 00:22:56,860
Where there is strength,

297
00:22:57,600 --> 00:22:58,760
there is weakness.

298
00:22:59,680 --> 00:23:00,810
Where there is gain,

299
00:23:02,140 --> 00:23:03,570
there is giving.

300
00:23:04,470 --> 00:23:05,610
Because in the end,

301
00:23:07,050 --> 00:23:09,310
everything depends on everything else.

302
00:23:12,370 --> 00:23:13,520
So...

303
00:23:16,100 --> 00:23:18,730
Phatsa, help my dad fulfill his dream.

304
00:23:23,550 --> 00:23:25,150
He wants to be a grandfather.

305
00:23:30,230 --> 00:23:31,010
Why...

306
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:35,870
is everyone talking about
pregnancy lately?

307
00:23:44,890 --> 00:23:46,830
Because you're cute, Phatsa.

308
00:23:52,350 --> 00:23:54,150
If it's a child you give birth to,

309
00:23:56,670 --> 00:23:57,570
I think...

310
00:24:00,190 --> 00:24:01,990
they'd definitely be very cute.

311
00:24:09,160 --> 00:24:12,140
Come on...

312
00:24:24,300 --> 00:24:25,260
Thank you.

313
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:28,930
Before,

314
00:24:31,500 --> 00:24:34,270
I never had faith in our relationship.

315
00:24:38,210 --> 00:24:40,010
The first day I met you, I bit you.

316
00:24:41,390 --> 00:24:43,040
That was really bad.

317
00:24:44,290 --> 00:24:45,090
It's the worst thing

318
00:24:45,090 --> 00:24:46,770
an Alpha can do to an Omega.

319
00:24:48,200 --> 00:24:50,050
Plus this damned bond

320
00:24:51,740 --> 00:24:53,140
forcing a framework on us

321
00:24:54,260 --> 00:24:55,790
before we even fell in love,

322
00:24:59,850 --> 00:25:01,580
binding the two of us together.

323
00:25:04,250 --> 00:25:04,980
In the past,

324
00:25:06,330 --> 00:25:07,440
I thought

325
00:25:09,710 --> 00:25:11,640
fate was playing tricks on people,

326
00:25:12,430 --> 00:25:14,320
tying a knot I didn't want

327
00:25:15,900 --> 00:25:17,610
onto the two of us.

328
00:25:20,200 --> 00:25:21,730
But because you're Phatsa,

329
00:25:23,380 --> 00:25:24,400
strong,

330
00:25:25,770 --> 00:25:26,620
smart,

331
00:25:28,610 --> 00:25:29,910
and gentle.

332
00:25:31,200 --> 00:25:32,840
I don't know when it started,

333
00:25:34,480 --> 00:25:36,010
but I always looked for you.

334
00:25:38,100 --> 00:25:39,690
I thought about you all day.

335
00:25:43,920 --> 00:25:45,920
I thought it was because of the bond,

336
00:25:49,820 --> 00:25:50,770
but it wasn't.

337
00:25:55,720 --> 00:25:57,720
It's because I fell in love with you.

338
00:25:58,910 --> 00:26:04,700
♪ I close my eyes, and it's all you ♪

339
00:26:04,720 --> 00:26:10,700
♪ Bound by your shadow, lost in dreams ♪

340
00:26:10,720 --> 00:26:15,040
♪ Sinking deep, nowhere to run ♪

341
00:26:11,940 --> 00:26:14,900
I don't really understand either,

342
00:26:14,920 --> 00:26:16,340
but

343
00:26:15,070 --> 00:26:18,520
♪ Only your words echo ♪

344
00:26:17,760 --> 00:26:19,440
because that person is you,

345
00:26:18,540 --> 00:26:22,030
♪ That we're in love ♪

346
00:26:21,090 --> 00:26:22,950
the bond that tied us together

347
00:26:22,050 --> 00:26:27,210
♪ But I don't even know if it's true ♪

348
00:26:24,190 --> 00:26:26,040
wasn't too painful.

349
00:26:27,190 --> 00:26:28,880
I probably

350
00:26:31,100 --> 00:26:32,500
fell in love with you too.

351
00:26:45,690 --> 00:26:47,340
Am I not dreaming?

352
00:26:50,060 --> 00:26:51,400
If it's a dream,

353
00:26:52,600 --> 00:26:54,260
then it's

354
00:26:55,320 --> 00:26:57,120
a dream I don't want to wake from.

355
00:27:09,870 --> 00:27:16,240
♪ I close my eyes, and it's all you ♪

356
00:27:10,890 --> 00:27:13,000
I want to remember every second

357
00:27:14,150 --> 00:27:15,630
of tonight.

358
00:27:16,270 --> 00:27:22,190
♪ Bound by your shadow, lost in dreams ♪

359
00:27:17,450 --> 00:27:18,580
Then

360
00:27:20,420 --> 00:27:22,420
just remember tonight well.

361
00:27:22,220 --> 00:27:26,130
♪ Sinking deep, nowhere to run ♪

362
00:27:25,690 --> 00:27:26,840
Stay by my side.

363
00:27:26,160 --> 00:27:29,550
♪ Only your words echo ♪

364
00:27:29,460 --> 00:27:30,800
Actually,

365
00:27:29,570 --> 00:27:33,320
♪ That we're in love ♪

366
00:27:32,010 --> 00:27:33,640
I'm really tired,

367
00:27:33,340 --> 00:27:36,150
♪ But I don't even know if it's true ♪

368
00:27:34,710 --> 00:27:35,640
but now

369
00:27:36,170 --> 00:27:39,870
♪ I close my eyes, and it's all you ♪

370
00:27:38,680 --> 00:27:40,180
I don't want to go anywhere.

371
00:27:39,900 --> 00:27:45,610
♪ Bound by your shadow, lost in dreams ♪

372
00:27:41,530 --> 00:27:42,840
I want to be with you.

373
00:27:45,630 --> 00:27:49,910
♪ Sinking deep, nowhere to run ♪

374
00:27:47,460 --> 00:27:48,990
You're not going anywhere.

375
00:27:49,930 --> 00:27:52,840
♪ Only your words echo ♪

376
00:27:50,470 --> 00:27:52,070
Then stay here with me, okay?

377
00:27:52,870 --> 00:27:56,510
♪ That we're in love ♪

378
00:27:56,530 --> 00:28:02,800
♪ But I don't even know if it's true ♪

379
00:27:58,550 --> 00:28:02,400
Then from now on, whether it's work,

380
00:28:03,280 --> 00:28:06,780
home, or our matters,

381
00:28:08,590 --> 00:28:11,960
you won't have to carry them
alone anymore.

382
00:28:27,920 --> 00:28:29,340
Then from now on,

383
00:28:32,400 --> 00:28:34,120
you must also remember

384
00:28:37,380 --> 00:28:39,160
you are no longer alone either.

385
00:36:23,340 --> 00:36:24,320
Dear.

386
00:36:25,190 --> 00:36:25,950
I'm here.

387
00:36:28,570 --> 00:36:30,230
Are you going to knot me again?

388
00:36:39,080 --> 00:36:40,390
Let me knot you.

389
00:36:48,350 --> 00:36:49,720
-Oh!
-Oh!

390
00:37:41,570 --> 00:37:44,670
[3 months later]

391
00:37:48,440 --> 00:37:51,390
Yongphat Company...

392
00:37:54,090 --> 00:37:55,570
Yongphat Company...

393
00:38:00,790 --> 00:38:01,880
Mr. Phatsa!

394
00:38:05,980 --> 00:38:07,100
The landowner of the land from earlier

395
00:38:07,100 --> 00:38:08,900
has agreed to sign the easement.

396
00:38:11,910 --> 00:38:13,020
Thank you.

397
00:38:13,180 --> 00:38:16,000
And the land you're worried about...

398
00:38:16,020 --> 00:38:17,950
I checked it. It's not landlocked.

399
00:38:19,100 --> 00:38:22,360
The easement remains valid
even if the landowner changes.

400
00:38:22,590 --> 00:38:23,600
Thank you.

401
00:38:24,480 --> 00:38:27,530
Then all the documents are complete.

402
00:38:28,920 --> 00:38:31,240
Ai, please take it to Sila

403
00:38:31,260 --> 00:38:32,700
and Nakhun to sign them.

404
00:38:32,720 --> 00:38:33,580
Okay.

405
00:38:33,610 --> 00:38:34,910
Thank you very much.

406
00:38:37,130 --> 00:38:39,890
Mr. Phatsa, since you came to help,

407
00:38:39,910 --> 00:38:42,370
the company's situation
has improved a lot.

408
00:38:42,950 --> 00:38:44,520
Mr. Nakhun is so lucky

409
00:38:45,010 --> 00:38:46,750
to have such a capable wife.

410
00:38:48,830 --> 00:38:50,370
You're exaggerating.

411
00:38:50,790 --> 00:38:52,510
I'm just doing my best.

412
00:38:52,710 --> 00:38:54,580
I'm still learning.

413
00:38:55,380 --> 00:38:57,440
But even so, this is already amazing.

414
00:38:57,600 --> 00:38:58,790
Thank you, Ai.

415
00:39:02,030 --> 00:39:03,980
Oh, right.

416
00:39:05,040 --> 00:39:07,040
Have you made a new friend recently?

417
00:39:07,080 --> 00:39:08,460
Yes.

418
00:39:08,980 --> 00:39:09,910
How is it?

419
00:39:11,090 --> 00:39:12,160
Pretty good.

420
00:39:13,310 --> 00:39:14,450
We just met.

421
00:39:14,900 --> 00:39:16,160
He's handsome, right?

422
00:39:17,100 --> 00:39:17,770
Yes.

423
00:39:19,300 --> 00:39:21,820
That smile is up to something, huh?

424
00:39:21,850 --> 00:39:24,310
It's rare to meet someone
you get along with.

425
00:39:24,660 --> 00:39:26,530
Then where is he?

426
00:39:27,210 --> 00:39:28,380
Probably at work.

427
00:39:29,640 --> 00:39:31,670
You guys are always together.

428
00:39:34,790 --> 00:39:35,910
Oh, Mr. Nakhun.

429
00:39:37,900 --> 00:39:39,560
What brings you here, Nakhun?

430
00:39:39,590 --> 00:39:40,510
Are you tired?

431
00:39:41,800 --> 00:39:42,900
No.

432
00:39:43,220 --> 00:39:44,710
Even if you're not tired,

433
00:39:45,700 --> 00:39:47,150
remember to eat and rest.

434
00:39:48,650 --> 00:39:49,540
Or

435
00:39:50,740 --> 00:39:52,530
you were so busy

436
00:39:53,440 --> 00:39:55,500
that you forgot your promise with me?

437
00:39:55,950 --> 00:39:57,350
No.

438
00:39:58,130 --> 00:40:00,040
I just finished talking with Ai.

439
00:40:00,770 --> 00:40:03,570
I was going to find you
once things wrapped up here,

440
00:40:03,830 --> 00:40:05,750
but you came to me first.

441
00:40:09,660 --> 00:40:10,380
I really don't want you

442
00:40:10,380 --> 00:40:11,450
to work so hard.

443
00:40:12,770 --> 00:40:13,990
I even

444
00:40:16,660 --> 00:40:18,410
don't want you to work.

445
00:40:20,470 --> 00:40:21,970
I want you to do nothing

446
00:40:22,830 --> 00:40:24,370
and just sit and smile at me.

447
00:40:28,600 --> 00:40:30,270
No way.

448
00:40:30,290 --> 00:40:32,910
If I sit around doing nothing all day,

449
00:40:33,290 --> 00:40:34,540
I'll become useless.

450
00:40:37,310 --> 00:40:38,520
I know

451
00:40:39,380 --> 00:40:41,750
you're amazing

452
00:40:42,490 --> 00:40:44,080
and capable.

453
00:40:44,110 --> 00:40:45,580
That's why I let you do it.

454
00:40:46,150 --> 00:40:47,720
And you're doing it well,

455
00:40:49,300 --> 00:40:50,310
right?

456
00:41:02,740 --> 00:41:04,570
I just finished my work.

457
00:41:06,350 --> 00:41:08,890
I think we should go eat.

458
00:41:08,920 --> 00:41:11,500
You must be hungry.

459
00:41:11,910 --> 00:41:12,810
But...

460
00:41:14,180 --> 00:41:16,240
it's too far to get to the restaurant.

461
00:41:16,960 --> 00:41:18,540
How about letting Jim

462
00:41:19,040 --> 00:41:20,700
cook something for you first?

463
00:41:30,950 --> 00:41:32,030
Can I eat you?

464
00:41:41,010 --> 00:41:42,610
You're being naughty again.

465
00:41:42,990 --> 00:41:44,380
How can you eat me?

466
00:41:44,880 --> 00:41:46,080
Why not?

467
00:41:46,810 --> 00:41:50,160
No. Why are you so dirty-minded?

468
00:41:52,160 --> 00:41:54,020
Being dirty-minded with my wife,

469
00:41:54,360 --> 00:41:55,890
what's strange about that?

470
00:41:58,700 --> 00:41:59,370
Am I right?

471
00:42:03,300 --> 00:42:05,950
I'm very spicy, you know.
Can you handle it?

472
00:42:08,440 --> 00:42:10,190
How spicy can it be?

473
00:42:11,890 --> 00:42:13,690
You definitely can't handle it.

474
00:42:14,640 --> 00:42:15,570
Well...

475
00:42:16,110 --> 00:42:17,440
Let me take a bite first.

476
00:42:19,520 --> 00:42:20,510
May I?

477
00:42:21,870 --> 00:42:22,780
No.

478
00:42:24,510 --> 00:42:25,600
Just a little.

479
00:42:27,940 --> 00:42:28,990
A little.

480
00:42:34,660 --> 00:42:35,880
Then go eat.

481
00:42:36,890 --> 00:42:39,600
Then let's go eat.

482
00:42:51,580 --> 00:42:52,630
Thank you.

483
00:42:55,350 --> 00:42:56,240
Here you are.

484
00:42:57,830 --> 00:43:00,490
What do you want to eat?
Order whatever you like.

485
00:43:08,210 --> 00:43:09,460
Well,

486
00:43:10,550 --> 00:43:12,010
I want...

487
00:43:15,400 --> 00:43:16,800
Raw Shrimp in Fish Sauce.

488
00:43:17,950 --> 00:43:18,600
Mm.

489
00:43:19,570 --> 00:43:20,880
And...

490
00:43:21,430 --> 00:43:23,810
This... Creamy Tom Yum Goong.

491
00:43:24,370 --> 00:43:27,240
Spicy Seafood Salad. For dessert,

492
00:43:27,270 --> 00:43:28,760
Coconut Milk Dessert.

493
00:43:30,150 --> 00:43:31,950
Wait.

494
00:43:33,070 --> 00:43:34,610
Raw Shrimp in Fish Sauce,

495
00:43:35,650 --> 00:43:39,120
Tom Yum Goong, and dessert?

496
00:43:42,170 --> 00:43:44,280
You don't eat desserts, do you?

497
00:43:44,640 --> 00:43:46,090
Neither do I.

498
00:43:47,810 --> 00:43:49,140
Who did you order it for?

499
00:43:50,410 --> 00:43:51,520
Exactly.

500
00:43:53,670 --> 00:43:54,360
I don't know why either.

501
00:43:54,360 --> 00:43:57,220
I suddenly feel like
eating something sweet today.

502
00:44:04,260 --> 00:44:08,620
Oh, maybe you have low blood sugar.

503
00:44:10,410 --> 00:44:12,210
You should eat something sweet.

504
00:44:12,880 --> 00:44:14,480
That way you'll have energy.

505
00:44:14,940 --> 00:44:16,660
Just now there was also this.

506
00:44:16,690 --> 00:44:18,650
This.

507
00:44:19,190 --> 00:44:20,440
Your favorite dish,

508
00:44:21,870 --> 00:44:23,480
Beef Massaman Curry.

509
00:44:24,850 --> 00:44:26,920
But later,

510
00:44:27,090 --> 00:44:28,890
let's order it without peanuts.

511
00:44:30,090 --> 00:44:31,150
I think

512
00:44:31,910 --> 00:44:34,640
this restaurant probably
doesn't have cashews.

513
00:44:35,270 --> 00:44:36,070
Do you want it?

514
00:44:37,150 --> 00:44:37,830
Yes.

515
00:44:39,280 --> 00:44:41,620
Hello, please order.

516
00:44:43,140 --> 00:44:44,370
What would you like?

517
00:44:44,400 --> 00:44:47,270
Raw Shrimp in Fish Sauce,

518
00:44:47,590 --> 00:44:50,620
Creamy Tom Yum Goong,
Spicy Seafood Salad,

519
00:44:50,950 --> 00:44:52,540
and Beef Massaman Curry.

520
00:44:53,250 --> 00:44:56,070
Oh, and no peanuts, please.

521
00:44:56,090 --> 00:44:58,560
Coconut Milk Dessert for dessert.

522
00:45:00,050 --> 00:45:01,690
That's all.

523
00:45:01,710 --> 00:45:03,190
Okay, I'll take the menu.

524
00:45:03,210 --> 00:45:04,910
Okay, thank you.

525
00:45:10,350 --> 00:45:12,430
You need to take good care
of yourself too.

526
00:45:12,430 --> 00:45:14,090
You even have low blood sugar.

527
00:45:14,370 --> 00:45:15,840
I do take care of myself.

528
00:45:17,490 --> 00:45:19,620
Otherwise how could I take care of you?

529
00:45:20,850 --> 00:45:22,580
You just take care of yourself.

530
00:45:22,820 --> 00:45:24,260
I can take care of myself.

531
00:45:25,420 --> 00:45:26,720
I'm strong.

532
00:45:32,380 --> 00:45:33,380
A few days ago,

533
00:45:34,170 --> 00:45:35,260
I had Nakhin go talk to

534
00:45:35,260 --> 00:45:37,520
the landowner of the Phatthanakan land.

535
00:45:38,810 --> 00:45:40,340
I want you to come along too.

536
00:45:40,940 --> 00:45:42,600
Maybe you'll have some ideas.

537
00:45:44,360 --> 00:45:45,720
Stop it.

538
00:45:49,720 --> 00:45:51,430
How much are you going to work?

539
00:45:53,170 --> 00:45:56,230
You're talking about work
even when we're going to eat.

540
00:45:56,670 --> 00:45:57,840
Besides,

541
00:45:58,720 --> 00:46:01,140
let me do things myself.

542
00:46:05,440 --> 00:46:07,330
I'm not doing that much now.

543
00:46:09,100 --> 00:46:10,550
With Nakhin helping,

544
00:46:11,860 --> 00:46:13,070
and you helping...

545
00:46:14,570 --> 00:46:15,480
Soon,

546
00:46:16,500 --> 00:46:18,030
Naphitch will graduate too

547
00:46:18,650 --> 00:46:20,340
and officially join to help.

548
00:46:21,870 --> 00:46:22,980
By then,

549
00:46:24,990 --> 00:46:27,250
I probably won't have to do
as much as now.

550
00:46:30,360 --> 00:46:32,090
Then...

551
00:46:34,140 --> 00:46:35,470
what are you going to do?

552
00:46:43,670 --> 00:46:46,130
I'm going to retire
and take care of our kids.

553
00:46:51,640 --> 00:46:52,480
What?

554
00:46:54,180 --> 00:46:57,270
Who said I was going to have kids for you?

555
00:47:02,770 --> 00:47:04,540
Ever since I knotted you,

556
00:47:06,470 --> 00:47:08,530
I haven't had any rut reaction at all.

557
00:47:10,890 --> 00:47:12,510
Don't you think

558
00:47:18,520 --> 00:47:20,240
you will give me a baby?

559
00:47:25,860 --> 00:47:27,410
Who knows?

560
00:47:29,020 --> 00:47:30,640
I've never been pregnant.

561
00:47:32,400 --> 00:47:35,140
And I don't know

562
00:47:35,160 --> 00:47:37,890
what it would be like for an Omega

563
00:47:38,580 --> 00:47:39,840
like me to be pregnant.

564
00:47:49,030 --> 00:47:51,090
You don't want to have a child with me?

565
00:47:52,790 --> 00:47:54,650
If you don't want to get pregnant,

566
00:47:55,530 --> 00:47:56,930
let's talk about it.

567
00:48:00,360 --> 00:48:01,550
No.

568
00:48:04,810 --> 00:48:06,270
I think I know

569
00:48:07,790 --> 00:48:10,170
pregnancy is pretty scary.

570
00:48:12,520 --> 00:48:13,630
But

571
00:48:16,260 --> 00:48:17,620
if it's our child,

572
00:48:20,040 --> 00:48:21,550
I also hope

573
00:48:22,540 --> 00:48:24,270
that child is yours.

574
00:48:31,070 --> 00:48:31,920
Really?

575
00:48:33,070 --> 00:48:34,080
Mm.

576
00:48:57,360 --> 00:48:58,390
Is it good?

577
00:48:59,190 --> 00:49:00,390
Extremely good.

578
00:49:00,710 --> 00:49:02,230
Let's eat together, Phatsa.

579
00:49:02,230 --> 00:49:03,710
You eat first.

580
00:49:04,140 --> 00:49:05,290
Eat more.

581
00:49:14,240 --> 00:49:15,510
Your favorite is here.

582
00:49:27,150 --> 00:49:29,780
Nakhun, what's wrong?

583
00:49:32,280 --> 00:49:34,280
So smelly. I feel a little nauseous.

584
00:49:45,180 --> 00:49:47,380
Phatsa, take the curry out first, okay?

585
00:49:47,690 --> 00:49:48,300
Huh?

586
00:49:48,330 --> 00:49:50,970
I'm dizzy and want to throw up.

587
00:49:52,240 --> 00:49:53,190
Ugh!

588
00:50:02,720 --> 00:50:03,900
It's not smelly.

589
00:50:03,920 --> 00:50:06,100
I feel dizzy.

590
00:50:07,550 --> 00:50:08,710
Take it out.

591
00:50:12,510 --> 00:50:13,830
Thanwa.

592
00:50:13,850 --> 00:50:14,390
Yes.

593
00:50:14,410 --> 00:50:15,340
Please take it away.

594
00:50:15,340 --> 00:50:16,080
Okay.

595
00:50:19,170 --> 00:50:20,770
Feeling better?

596
00:50:21,440 --> 00:50:23,660
Mr. Phatsa, here's water.

597
00:50:24,280 --> 00:50:25,340
Thank you.

598
00:50:25,360 --> 00:50:26,750
Have some water.

599
00:50:47,710 --> 00:50:48,980
Lemon water?

600
00:50:51,210 --> 00:50:52,340
It's for Mr. Nakhun.

601
00:50:53,580 --> 00:50:54,530
Are we going to keep doing this,

602
00:50:54,530 --> 00:50:56,590
finding these things for Mr. Nakhun?

603
00:50:57,030 --> 00:50:58,410
Our duty

604
00:50:58,440 --> 00:50:59,490
is to care for and protect

605
00:50:59,490 --> 00:51:01,100
Mr. Nakhun and Mr. Phatsa.

606
00:51:04,640 --> 00:51:08,660
I'm new here. Please teach me more.

607
00:51:11,160 --> 00:51:13,190
Then stay by my side more.

608
00:51:14,460 --> 00:51:15,090
Let's go.

609
00:51:26,630 --> 00:51:27,560
Mr. Nakhun,

610
00:51:31,100 --> 00:51:32,190
Drink a little.

611
00:51:55,140 --> 00:51:56,150
Are you better?

612
00:51:58,610 --> 00:51:59,760
A little.

613
00:52:02,320 --> 00:52:04,450
Maybe some nasal inhaler, Mr. Phatsa?

614
00:52:07,060 --> 00:52:08,460
Thank you.

615
00:52:09,020 --> 00:52:11,770
Smell it and you'll feel better.

616
00:52:13,710 --> 00:52:15,600
No.

617
00:52:16,270 --> 00:52:17,360
I want to smell you.

618
00:52:25,850 --> 00:52:26,590
Thank you very much.

619
00:52:26,590 --> 00:52:27,520
You're welcome.

620
00:52:33,230 --> 00:52:34,940
Does it help?

621
00:52:36,630 --> 00:52:37,850
Better.

622
00:53:14,730 --> 00:53:16,160
What's wrong?

623
00:53:17,090 --> 00:53:19,920
Is this smelly too?

624
00:53:24,030 --> 00:53:24,960
No.

625
00:53:27,050 --> 00:53:28,220
On the clothes,

626
00:53:30,310 --> 00:53:32,040
there's someone else's scent.

627
00:53:36,500 --> 00:53:37,570
It's like

628
00:53:39,010 --> 00:53:39,930
your scent

629
00:53:42,160 --> 00:53:43,660
mixed with mine.

630
00:54:02,440 --> 00:54:03,700
Do you like it, Phatsa?

631
00:54:05,730 --> 00:54:06,420
I like it quite a lot.

632
00:54:06,420 --> 00:54:07,020
Nakhun...

633
00:54:08,900 --> 00:54:09,980
But

634
00:54:10,850 --> 00:54:13,030
this land is so close to the lake.

635
00:54:14,600 --> 00:54:16,590
It must be terribly expensive.

636
00:54:18,580 --> 00:54:19,710
Not that expensive.

637
00:54:20,140 --> 00:54:22,390
And the landowner won't sell it to us.

638
00:54:24,230 --> 00:54:26,230
He asked us to help think of a project

639
00:54:27,060 --> 00:54:29,340
to develop the value of this area.

640
00:54:31,140 --> 00:54:32,480
If it were you,

641
00:54:34,540 --> 00:54:35,940
what would you want to do?

642
00:54:40,780 --> 00:54:43,030
This location is great.

643
00:54:45,890 --> 00:54:46,670
But

644
00:54:48,570 --> 00:54:50,210
with the land in front,

645
00:54:51,150 --> 00:54:52,870
there definitely will be traffic jams.

646
00:54:52,870 --> 00:54:54,570
The road only has two lanes.

647
00:54:57,440 --> 00:54:59,540
Although we can use the waterway,

648
00:55:01,650 --> 00:55:04,390
in the end we'd still need private boats.

649
00:55:05,580 --> 00:55:09,060
And we'd probably
have to build a pier ourselves.

650
00:55:10,350 --> 00:55:11,640
Good analysis.

651
00:55:16,560 --> 00:55:20,010
Well... What if it were you?

652
00:55:21,280 --> 00:55:22,980
What would you do here?

653
00:55:26,260 --> 00:55:27,740
If it were me...

654
00:55:30,530 --> 00:55:31,630
This land

655
00:55:32,800 --> 00:55:34,960
is close to a big mall,

656
00:55:36,450 --> 00:55:37,450
close to a market,

657
00:55:38,290 --> 00:55:39,490
and close to a temple.

658
00:55:40,810 --> 00:55:42,090
If it were me,

659
00:55:44,530 --> 00:55:45,860
I would build a hotel.

660
00:55:59,820 --> 00:56:01,120
What are you building?

661
00:56:02,910 --> 00:56:03,840
A hotel.

662
00:56:07,040 --> 00:56:07,660
Phatsa.

663
00:56:12,950 --> 00:56:13,520
Phatsa.

664
00:56:17,410 --> 00:56:18,140
Phatsa.

665
00:56:21,220 --> 00:56:21,940
Phatsa!

666
00:56:23,440 --> 00:56:24,730
Why are you crying?

667
00:56:25,730 --> 00:56:27,670
Phatsa.

668
00:56:28,460 --> 00:56:29,510
Phatsa.

669
00:56:31,670 --> 00:56:33,050
Phatsa.

670
00:56:33,070 --> 00:56:34,960
Phatsa.

671
00:56:37,880 --> 00:56:38,730
Phatsa.

672
00:56:40,190 --> 00:56:41,230
What's wrong?

673
00:56:48,650 --> 00:56:52,060
Don't build a hotel.

674
00:56:52,430 --> 00:56:55,710
Why do you want to build a hotel?

675
00:56:58,860 --> 00:57:00,120
What's wrong, Phatsa?

676
00:57:03,630 --> 00:57:05,730
No!

677
00:57:06,270 --> 00:57:08,580
Don't build a hotel.

678
00:57:10,660 --> 00:57:12,540
Sorry, we won't build a hotel.

679
00:57:12,560 --> 00:57:14,170
We won't do it.

680
00:57:14,200 --> 00:57:15,470
Don't cry, Phatsa.

681
00:57:20,780 --> 00:57:22,730
Really not building a hotel?

682
00:57:23,530 --> 00:57:24,460
Not building it.

683
00:57:24,530 --> 00:57:26,090
Don't cry, Phatsa.

684
00:57:28,020 --> 00:57:29,690
When you cry, my heart breaks.

685
00:57:35,580 --> 00:57:37,770
Then why did you mention the hotel?

686
00:57:53,090 --> 00:57:53,980
Phatsa.

687
00:57:56,920 --> 00:57:58,380
Can I ask?

688
00:58:01,270 --> 00:58:03,110
Why can't I build a hotel?

689
00:58:04,710 --> 00:58:05,360
Just...

690
00:58:07,810 --> 00:58:09,310
You said

691
00:58:11,210 --> 00:58:14,740
you once went to a hotel
and slept with someone else, didn't you?

692
00:58:15,490 --> 00:58:17,050
I don't like it.

693
00:58:21,280 --> 00:58:21,960
Phatsa.

694
00:58:23,520 --> 00:58:24,800
Listen to me.

695
00:58:28,540 --> 00:58:29,860
I don't want you

696
00:58:29,880 --> 00:58:32,140
to misunderstand about the hotel again.

697
00:58:34,150 --> 00:58:35,190
I love you.

698
00:58:36,770 --> 00:58:37,970
I only love you.

699
00:58:40,530 --> 00:58:42,260
The hotel I'm going to build...

700
00:58:43,780 --> 00:58:45,310
I will only be there with you

701
00:58:46,510 --> 00:58:48,370
And I will only sleep with you too.

702
00:58:54,070 --> 00:58:55,530
This hotel is built for you

703
00:58:56,770 --> 00:58:58,430
to erase

704
00:58:59,150 --> 00:59:00,330
those bad memories.

705
00:59:04,260 --> 00:59:05,590
Phatsa, trust me, okay?

706
00:59:20,340 --> 00:59:22,350
I'm sorry. I was too unreasonable.

707
00:59:25,700 --> 00:59:27,920
I don't know what's wrong with me either.

708
00:59:27,920 --> 00:59:29,990
The tears just came out on their own.

709
00:59:33,760 --> 00:59:34,710
Don't cry.

710
00:59:40,290 --> 00:59:41,820
If you are sad,

711
00:59:42,220 --> 00:59:43,480
I won't say it again.

712
00:59:45,060 --> 00:59:47,500
I won't go to a hotel without you.

713
00:59:50,250 --> 00:59:52,340
But I just want you to know,

714
00:59:53,980 --> 00:59:55,540
and to believe,

715
00:59:57,080 --> 00:59:58,500
that I only love you.

716
01:00:01,550 --> 01:00:03,070
I love you so much.

717
01:00:04,830 --> 01:00:06,590
How could I have someone else?

718
01:00:23,750 --> 01:00:25,100
I'm sorry.

719
01:00:26,870 --> 01:00:28,500
I apologize to you too.

720
01:00:36,530 --> 01:00:37,570
Don't cry.

721
01:00:55,570 --> 01:00:56,900
Are you feeling better?

722
01:00:57,120 --> 01:00:57,990
Yes.

723
01:01:00,510 --> 01:01:01,960
Phatsa! Phatsa!

724
01:01:01,990 --> 01:01:02,650
Phatsa!

725
01:01:03,600 --> 01:01:04,560
Phatsa!

726
01:01:09,510 --> 01:01:10,130
Phatsa.

727
01:01:17,360 --> 01:01:18,270
How are you?

728
01:01:19,240 --> 01:01:20,500
Does it hurt anywhere?

729
01:01:22,310 --> 01:01:24,030
A little headache.

730
01:01:27,080 --> 01:01:28,540
But it should be fine soon.

731
01:01:30,000 --> 01:01:31,730
You don't have to work anymore.

732
01:01:33,330 --> 01:01:34,400
Do nothing.

733
01:01:35,470 --> 01:01:37,000
Just let me take care of you.

734
01:01:47,130 --> 01:01:48,030
No.

735
01:01:51,460 --> 01:01:53,160
If you let me do nothing,

736
01:01:54,550 --> 01:01:56,440
I'll rot away.

737
01:02:00,920 --> 01:02:02,650
I just feel a little dizzy.

738
01:02:04,700 --> 01:02:06,290
It should get better soon.

739
01:02:09,130 --> 01:02:10,610
Mr. Nakhun, Mr. Phatsa.

740
01:02:10,900 --> 01:02:12,470
The doctor is here.

741
01:02:17,220 --> 01:02:18,270
Doctor.

742
01:02:19,650 --> 01:02:21,330
What exactly is wrong with Phatsa?

743
01:02:21,330 --> 01:02:23,080
Mr. Nakhun, calm down first.

744
01:02:23,110 --> 01:02:25,640
Mr. Phatsa doesn't have
any serious illness.

745
01:02:25,830 --> 01:02:27,760
But Phatsa fainted!

746
01:02:28,970 --> 01:02:30,950
He's usually in good health!

747
01:02:31,550 --> 01:02:33,760
Doctor, don't lie to me!

748
01:02:37,410 --> 01:02:38,710
Mr. Nakhun.

749
01:02:39,580 --> 01:02:40,620
Stop!

750
01:02:43,710 --> 01:02:45,330
I already told you before!

751
01:02:53,380 --> 01:02:54,260
I'm sorry.

752
01:02:55,520 --> 01:02:57,650
I also want to apologize to the doctor.

753
01:02:59,030 --> 01:03:00,220
I...

754
01:03:01,890 --> 01:03:03,590
was too worried about you.

755
01:03:06,180 --> 01:03:07,190
It's okay.

756
01:03:09,630 --> 01:03:11,490
I think we should calm down first.

757
01:03:11,770 --> 01:03:13,550
Maybe it's nothing serious.

758
01:03:15,560 --> 01:03:16,830
Mr. Phatsa

759
01:03:16,860 --> 01:03:18,670
fainted because he's tired.

760
01:03:18,690 --> 01:03:20,040
And most importantly,

761
01:03:20,060 --> 01:03:22,160
for someone who just got pregnant...

762
01:03:27,030 --> 01:03:28,190
Pregnant?

763
01:03:31,010 --> 01:03:32,520
Pregnant, Doctor?

764
01:03:32,800 --> 01:03:35,260
Is my wife pregnant?

765
01:03:35,280 --> 01:03:36,730
The blood test results show

766
01:03:36,730 --> 01:03:38,720
Mr. Phatsa is pregnant.

767
01:03:38,740 --> 01:03:42,340
As for the gestational age,
we'll need an ultrasound to confirm.

768
01:04:05,940 --> 01:04:07,100
Mr. Nakhun, Mr. Phatsa.

769
01:04:07,100 --> 01:04:08,360
Please don't go in yet.

770
01:04:08,480 --> 01:04:10,420
Now, Sila,

771
01:04:10,440 --> 01:04:11,760
Jim,

772
01:04:11,780 --> 01:04:13,010
and the butler, Chawe,

773
01:04:13,010 --> 01:04:14,850
are preparing to celebrate

774
01:04:15,370 --> 01:04:18,820
the new little master
of the Devathitirat family.

775
01:04:20,410 --> 01:04:22,250
Everyone is happy now,

776
01:04:22,840 --> 01:04:24,440
especially Ms. Kampirada

777
01:04:24,460 --> 01:04:25,620
and Mr. Nakhin.

778
01:04:26,110 --> 01:04:28,070
Mr. Naphitch even said

779
01:04:28,090 --> 01:04:31,490
he'll come back from Hong Kong next week
to celebrate with us.

780
01:04:32,370 --> 01:04:34,010
Congratulations.

781
01:04:34,740 --> 01:04:37,060
We two will go in first
to check the situation.

782
01:04:37,060 --> 01:04:37,980
Okay.

783
01:04:38,000 --> 01:04:39,350
Thank you.

784
01:04:46,840 --> 01:04:47,960
Nakhun.

785
01:04:50,180 --> 01:04:53,420
Why is everyone so excited?

786
01:04:55,070 --> 01:04:57,130
It's our family's first grandchild.

787
01:04:57,710 --> 01:04:59,660
Of course everyone is excited.

788
01:05:00,300 --> 01:05:02,600
And that's not even counting

789
01:05:03,750 --> 01:05:04,300
Phatsa

790
01:05:04,320 --> 01:05:05,320
being a Pure Omega

791
01:05:08,640 --> 01:05:10,360
and me being a True Alpha.

792
01:05:11,090 --> 01:05:12,600
Our child

793
01:05:12,620 --> 01:05:14,920
has a high chance of becoming an Enigma.

794
01:05:18,080 --> 01:05:20,310
I don't want them to be expected

795
01:05:21,090 --> 01:05:22,900
before they're even born.

796
01:05:23,210 --> 01:05:26,070
Those things about secondary gender

797
01:05:27,870 --> 01:05:29,470
deciding fate and status...

798
01:05:37,030 --> 01:05:38,340
Things like that

799
01:05:42,610 --> 01:05:44,470
are hard to control anyway.

800
01:05:47,740 --> 01:05:49,910
Then if

801
01:05:50,730 --> 01:05:52,290
they are not an Enigma

802
01:05:53,230 --> 01:05:54,210
or a True Alpha

803
01:05:54,230 --> 01:05:55,020
like you,

804
01:05:56,860 --> 01:05:59,420
will they still be loved just the same?

805
01:06:20,240 --> 01:06:22,200
Whether you are a boy

806
01:06:23,090 --> 01:06:24,110
or a girl,

807
01:06:25,410 --> 01:06:27,670
no matter what your secondary gender is,

808
01:06:29,160 --> 01:06:31,060
I want you to know

809
01:06:32,990 --> 01:06:34,320
that I love you the most.

810
01:06:35,610 --> 01:06:37,120
I will use my love

811
01:06:38,170 --> 01:06:39,370
and all of my strength

812
01:06:39,640 --> 01:06:40,750
to protect you,

813
01:06:41,950 --> 01:06:43,810
raise you,

814
01:06:44,370 --> 01:06:46,070
make our home warm,

815
01:06:48,500 --> 01:06:49,960
and it will always be this way.

816
01:06:49,960 --> 01:06:54,390
♪ There's no time ♪

817
01:06:59,020 --> 01:07:04,530
♪ It's so lonely ♪

818
01:07:06,560 --> 01:07:13,590
♪ I'm breathing in ♪

819
01:07:15,040 --> 01:07:22,420
♪ And breathe out together ♪

820
01:07:22,450 --> 01:07:27,420
♪ There's no time ♪

821
01:07:25,090 --> 01:07:26,360
Thank you.

822
01:07:28,790 --> 01:07:29,520
My pleasure.

823
01:07:31,780 --> 01:07:38,750
♪ There's no time ♪

824
01:07:31,960 --> 01:07:33,270
But...

825
01:07:34,160 --> 01:07:35,980
do you think this little one

826
01:07:37,230 --> 01:07:38,750
will be a girl or a boy?

827
01:07:39,770 --> 01:07:40,750
I think

828
01:07:42,630 --> 01:07:43,710
it should be twins.

829
01:07:45,250 --> 01:07:46,840
Twins?

830
01:07:48,830 --> 01:07:50,400
How could it be twins?

831
01:07:51,680 --> 01:07:53,750
After I knotted you,

832
01:07:54,690 --> 01:07:56,470
we've done it many times.

833
01:07:59,340 --> 01:08:01,360
Come on...

834
01:08:02,290 --> 01:08:05,220
Who gets pregnant again
while already pregnant?

835
01:08:06,380 --> 01:08:07,560
Nonsense...

836
01:08:11,380 --> 01:08:12,840
I'm not talking nonsense.

837
01:08:16,779 --> 01:08:18,220
But I really love you.

838
01:08:36,979 --> 01:08:38,790
Even if our relationship

839
01:08:40,240 --> 01:08:42,700
started with a fate that we can't control.

840
01:08:44,390 --> 01:08:46,399
I didn't mean to bite you.

841
01:08:48,279 --> 01:08:50,120
We formed a bond

842
01:08:51,279 --> 01:08:53,880
and the rules of soulmates
forced their way in.

843
01:08:54,470 --> 01:08:56,770
But I want you to know

844
01:08:57,760 --> 01:08:59,359
because you are you, Phatsa,

845
01:09:01,380 --> 01:09:02,920
not because of pheromones,

846
01:09:03,880 --> 01:09:06,210
not because of the bond formed between us,

847
01:09:09,979 --> 01:09:10,640
but because Phatsa

848
01:09:10,640 --> 01:09:11,470
is Phatsa,

849
01:09:13,850 --> 01:09:15,050
the one who is strong,

850
01:09:16,990 --> 01:09:17,859
smart,

851
01:09:19,520 --> 01:09:20,390
generous,

852
01:09:24,310 --> 01:09:25,500
and loves me.

853
01:09:39,729 --> 01:09:40,569
I love you.

854
01:09:40,600 --> 01:09:46,170
♪ I close my eyes, and it's all you ♪

855
01:09:46,210 --> 01:09:52,279
♪ Bound by your shadow, lost in dreams ♪

856
01:09:52,310 --> 01:09:56,540
♪ Sinking deep, nowhere to run ♪

857
01:09:56,570 --> 01:09:59,850
♪ Only your words echo ♪

858
01:09:59,870 --> 01:10:08,610
♪ That we're in love ♪

859
01:10:01,420 --> 01:10:03,530
I love you too,

860
01:10:04,490 --> 01:10:05,600
Daddy.

861
01:10:08,640 --> 01:10:14,620
♪ But I don't even know if it's true ♪

862
01:10:10,450 --> 01:10:11,450
Yeah.

863
01:10:24,740 --> 01:10:26,280
You finally became Daddy.

864
01:10:37,980 --> 01:10:39,150
Of course, my baby.

865
01:10:51,680 --> 01:10:57,220
♪ I close my eyes, and it's all you ♪

866
01:10:57,250 --> 01:11:03,410
♪ Bound by your shadow, lost in dreams ♪

867
01:11:03,430 --> 01:11:07,640
♪ Sinking deep, nowhere to run ♪

868
01:11:05,090 --> 01:11:12,410
[The end]

